  "title": "No, AMOC won’t collapse next year. **I’m reposting a video on the top...",
  "description": "No, AMOC won’t collapse next year. **I’m reposting a video on the topic I originally produced in July 2023 because there’s a few viral climate doom videos on the topic currently making their rounds on social media** The Atlantic Meridional Overturning Circulation, or AMOC for short, is a large system of ocean currents that influences climate in North America and Europe. It is currently slowing down, and several studies have theorized it could collapse if climate change is not addressed quickly enough.  The most recent statistical analysis, that I discuss in this video, points towards a collapse between 2050 and 2100, but it’s important to note that it isn’t widely accepted within the scientific community due to insufficient and discredited evidence. A collapse is still possible, but a recent IPCC suggests it wouldn’t occur as instantaneously and catastrophically like a lot of the media around it suggests. I’m looking at you, “Day After Tomorrow”.  Scientists agree that the best thing we can do to prevent irreversible tipping points, like AMOC collapsing, is to force the world to begin to phase out fossil fuels and transition funding from that industry into renewables. It won’t be easy, but it’s necessary to avoid the worst impacts of climate change. There are a bunch of easy calls to action to do just linked in my bio, so don’t give up! #ClimateChange #ClimateCrisis #ClimateEmergency #GlobalWarming #AMOC #AMOCCollapse #TippingPoint ",
